  "id": 22028,
  "link": "https://events.carleton.ca/event/the-biology-of-cancer/",
  "title": {
   "rendered": "The Biology of Cancer"
  },
  "content": {
   "rendered": "<header class=\"mb-6 cu-pageheader cu-component-updated md:mb-12\">\n    <h1 class=\"cu-prose-first-last font-semibold !mt-2 mb-4 md:mb-6 text-3xl md:text-4xl lg:text-5xl lg:leading-[3.5rem] relative after:absolute after:h-px after:bottom-0 pb-5 after:w-10 after:bg-cu-red after:left-px\">\n        \n    </h1>\n    \n        </header>\n\n    \n    \n    \n    \n            <div class=\"cu-buttongroup cu-component-updated flex flex-wrap md:flex-1 gap-3 md:gap-5 justify-start\">\n                                                                                                        </div>\n        \n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1024\" height=\"321\" src=\"https://events.carleton.ca/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Blurb-Images-1-1-1024x321.png\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-22030\" role=\"none\" srcset=\"https://events.carleton.ca/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Blurb-Images-1-1-1024x321.png 1024w, https://events.carleton.ca/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Blurb-Images-1-1-512x160.png 512w, https://events.carleton.ca/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Blurb-Images-1-1-320x100.png 320w, https://events.carleton.ca/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Blurb-Images-1-1-768x240.png 768w, https://events.carleton.ca/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Blurb-Images-1-1-1536x481.png 1536w, https://events.carleton.ca/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Blurb-Images-1-1.png 1920w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\" /></figure>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Cancer is a terrifying disease, yet we have made amazing progress in dealing with it over the past few decades. This course is offered as an introduction understanding how cancer develops, how cancer cells differ from normal cells and how we diagnose, classify and stage (extent of spread of the cancer) the common cancers. While the summary aspects of treatment will be discussed, this is not intended to focus on treatments. Special attention will be devoted to colon, breast, prostate and skin cancers. No previous knowledge of biology is necessary and while it is in a lecture format, questions and discussion is encouraged. </p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>This is a six-week course running Mondays, from November 2 to December 7, 2026, from 1:00PM to 3:00PM at Carleton Dominion-Chalmers Centre in downtown Ottawa.</strong></p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Part of CDCC’s <strong>Lifelong Learning</strong> program, the course is designed to bring people together to explore new ideas, connect with others, and keep learning at every stage of life.</p>\n\n\n",
   "protected": false
  },
